{"kind":"request","text":"PG-1: a typed stand-in grant for prediction, exported from\npackages/derive. One small head with checker review and the gate.\nIt is the work of planner request 944f9cad, which the owner asked\nfor on 12 November. Read 944f9cad for the facts at main 7ea170c9.\n\nScope. One exported function, for example\n`predictionGrant(definition, actor, scope)`. It returns a grant of\nevery declared action for one key, marked current, with no cast\nat the call site. Its documentation says that a prediction with\nit never answers `unauthorized`, and that the caller's clock\ndecides `expired`. The fixtures in packages/derive/test use the\nsame function in place of their cast.\n\nNo change to the judge's rules, to an entry or to the wire. If\nthe typed form needs `fresh` to be optional on a type, the note\nshows that no runtime path can pass a grant with no proof.\n\nWitness: a test shows that a prediction with the function equals\nthe entry that a scope seals for the same signed bytes.\n\nOrder. After the cutover head 05d618e2 lands. The cutover changes\nmost of packages/derive, and this head must not add to its merge.\nIt is the lowest of the three requests of 12 November.","body":{"conditions":"packages/derive exports one typed stand-in grant for prediction with no cast at the call site; its documentation states the unauthorized and expired limits; a test shows a prediction equals the sealed entry; no change to the judge, an entry or the wire; lands after the cutover head; checker review and the gate.","target_head":"2216316ea76f4df59413d42b916b3b66e1c02cb2","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}